---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { affiliates } from '../../site.config';
const active = affiliates.filter((a) => a.enabled && a.ref);
---
<Base
  title="Affiliate disclosure"
  description="How this site makes money, which links are affiliate links, and why that never affects the health scores."
  path="/disclosure"
>
  <div class="wrap narrow prose">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Affiliate disclosure' }]} />
    <h1>Affiliate disclosure</h1>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>
      Some links to hosting providers on this site are affiliate links. If you sign up through
      one, we may receive a commission. You pay exactly the same price — in several cases you get
      a signup credit that is not available otherwise.
    </p>

    <h2>What is never affected</h2>
    <p>
      Health scores, rankings and comparisons are computed by a script from public repository data.
      No software project pays to appear, to rank higher, or to be included. There is no mechanism
      by which they could: the ordering on every page is generated at build time from the score,
      and the score has no input a third party can influence.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not take payment from software projects at all — only from hosting providers, and only
      for signups that come from links clearly marked as sponsored.
    </p>

    <h2>Which links are affiliate links</h2>
    {active.length > 0 ? (
      <>
        <p>We currently participate in the affiliate programmes of:</p>
        <ul>{active.map((a) => <li>{a.name}</li>)}</ul>
        <p>
          Every such link carries <code>rel="sponsored"</code> in the page source, and appears
          inside a block labelled as hosting. Links to project websites, source code and
          documentation are never affiliate links.
        </p>
      </>
    ) : (
      <p>
        No affiliate programmes are active on this site at the moment. If that changes, this page
        lists every partner before any link goes live, and each sponsored link is marked in the
        page source with <code>rel="sponsored"</code>.
      </p>
    )}

    <h2>Why we say so</h2>
    <p>
      Because the US Federal Trade Commission requires it, because the EU Unfair Commercial
      Practices Directive requires it, and because a directory whose ordering you cannot trust is
      worth nothing. The scoring method is published in full on the
      <a href="/methodology">methodology page</a> so you can check the ranking yourself.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
